Boy, I don't know why everyone is so confused about this.  Even big
Dave couldn't give a clear explanation--not even in his cute little
quote.

There are three teleport "intrinsics" you can get.  They all do
different things.

teleport control:  when you get this, you can control exactly where
you appear when you teleport.  If you end up in a level teleport, you
can choose which level you want to go to.  This attribute is given by
a ring of tele control, eating a tengu (or the Wizard, but you
should already have it at that point), or playing a wizard character
and getting past the 17th level.  Note that you can not teleport onto
traps, into walls, over monsters, and so on.  If you try, you will be
teleported randomly.

can teleport:  simply means that you will randomly teleport every once
in awhile.  You don't get asked if you want to 'port.  It just
happens:  poof!  This can be really annoying if you are in a shop and
you haven't paid yet, and you don't like Kops.  It can also be
annoying when you are walking towards the exit and suddenly appear on
the other side of the screen.  It can be a lifesaver if you are being
chased, though.  One of these teleports can be controlled if you have
the teleport control intrinsic.  This teleport does not make you
hungrier.  This happens roughly every 100 turns.  I don't have the
exact numbers, but it is VERY unpredictable.  You get this intrinsic
by either wearing a ring of teleport or by eating a teleporting
creature (tengu, leprechaun, nymph, etc.).

can teleport at will:  means that you can teleport by typing a ^T, any
time you want.  If you fall into water, this is the only way to keep
from drowning, since the computer will attempt to do this for you
automatically.  This attribute is acquired simply by gaining enough
levels.  I'm not sure of the exact details of which character types
gain this attribute when, but it is somewhere around level 10.  This
teleport should be used sparingly, as it will quickly make your
character hungry.  When you are in a really tight spot, this is the
best one, since it doesn't require spells, scrolls, luck, or whatever.
Just type ^T and >poof!<.  It also saves a lot of time wandering around
Hell.  Also, if you suddenly need to not be satiated any more, pop off
a few of these.

A few further notes:

Here are some things that can teleport you involuntarily:
Quantum mechanics hitting you
reading a cursed spellbook
teleport traps
rings of teleport
teleport intrinsic
stepping in water when you have the voluntary teleport intrinsic
boss walking into room and about to see you playing NetHack

Here are the voluntary teleport methods:
reading a scroll of teleportation
zapping self with wand of teleportation
typing a ^T

Here are the things that can level teleport you:
stepping on a level teleport trap (always 1 use only)
reading a teleport scroll while confused
reading a cursed teleport scroll

There is a "pseudo-control" teleport trap in some closets.  It
teleports you to a vault.

Level teleport traps and trapdoors are often found in similar
situations, so be careful!

For a very limited teleport, try throwing a heavy iron ball while it
is attatched to your leg.  If you have enough strength, you can move
quite a distance!  Just the thing to put some distance between you and
that Jabberwock.  Certainly faster than dragging the damn thing
everywhere.  Cute effect if you're stuck in a bear trap.

There.  That should clear things up.

